## 2. Dock Appointment Scheduling

2.1 **Appointments are mandatory.** Every truck delivering to or collecting from an HPL facility must hold a confirmed dock appointment in the HPL Dock Scheduler. Trucks without an appointment are worked only if a dock is free and may wait until the end of the day.

2.2 **Slot length.** Appointments are booked in {{ f.dock_rules.slot_minutes }}-minute slots. A slot is available only if its status in the Dock Scheduler is "available"; slots marked "blocked" are out of service (for example for maintenance) and cannot be booked.

2.3 **Lead time.** Standard appointments must be booked at least {{ f.dock_rules.booking_lead_hours }} hours before the slot start time. Appointments for shipments containing hazardous materials must be booked at least {{ f.dock_rules.hazmat_booking_lead_hours }} hours in advance (see HPL-EHS-004).

2.4 **Hazmat docks.** Hazardous materials may only be loaded or unloaded at designated hazmat docks:
{% for w in f.warehouses %}
- {{ w.code }} ({{ w.name }}): {% if w.hazmat_docks %}dock{% if w.hazmat_docks|length > 1 %}s{% endif %} {{ w.hazmat_docks | join(" and ") }}{% else %}no hazmat docks - hazardous materials are not accepted at this facility{% endif %}{% endfor %}

2.5 **Carrier limits.** A single carrier may hold at most {{ f.dock_rules.max_slots_per_carrier_per_day }} appointments per facility per day, to keep dock capacity available for all partners.

2.6 **Rescheduling and cancellation.** Appointments may be moved or cancelled free of charge up to 4 hours before the slot start time. Later cancellations are treated as no-shows (Section 3.3).

## 3. Arrival and Check-in

3.1 Drivers should arrive 15 minutes before the appointment and check in at the gatehouse with: the BOL, the HPL shipment ID (SH-NNNNN), a valid driver's license and, for hazmat loads, the Safety Data Sheet (SDS) and emergency response information.

3.2 **Grace period.** A driver who checks in no later than {{ f.dock_rules.late_grace_minutes }} minutes after the appointment start is treated as on time.

3.3 **Late arrival and no-show.** A driver who arrives more than {{ f.dock_rules.late_grace_minutes }} minutes late forfeits the appointment. The carrier must book a new slot in the Dock Scheduler and may be charged a no-show fee of {{ f.dock_rules.no_show_fee_usd | usd }}. The same fee applies when a carrier does not arrive at all or cancels less than 4 hours ahead.

3.4 **Free time and detention.** HPL aims to complete loading or unloading within {{ f.dock_rules.free_time_hours }} hours of check-in. Carriers that checked in within the grace period may bill detention after {{ f.dock_rules.free_time_hours }} hours at {{ f.dock_rules.detention_usd_per_hour | usd }} per hour (see HPL-LEG-001, Section 5.6). Detention is not payable to drivers who arrived late.

## 4. Receiving

4.1 **Inspection.** Receivers check piece count, visible condition and seal number against the BOL before signing. Any shortage, overage or damage (OS&D) must be written on the delivery receipt before the driver leaves; see HPL-OPS-006 for claims.

4.2 **OS&D reporting.** OS&D findings are entered in the warehouse management system within 24 hours of receipt.

4.3 **Dock-to-stock.** Received goods must be put away and available for picking within {{ f.sla.dock_to_stock_hours }} hours of check-in.

4.4 **Rejected freight.** HPL refuses freight that is leaking, has damaged hazmat packaging, or exceeds the pallet limits of HPL-OPS-005 by more than 10%.

## 5. Outbound and Cut-off Times

5.1 **Same-day cut-off.** Orders released to the warehouse before {{ f.dock_rules.same_day_cutoff }} local time ship the same day. Orders released after {{ f.dock_rules.same_day_cutoff }} ship the next operating day of the facility.

5.2 **Carrier selection.** Outbound shipments are tendered to carriers listed in the HPL Carrier Registry that serve the destination zone and mode. Hazmat shipments may only be tendered to hazmat-certified carriers.

5.3 **Load verification.** Before the trailer is sealed, the loader scans every pallet or parcel label and confirms the count against the BOL.

## 6. Inventory Control

6.1 **Available quantity.** The quantity available to promise for a SKU is quantity on hand minus quantity reserved for open orders.

6.2 **Replenishment alerts.** When the quantity on hand of a SKU at a facility falls below its reorder point, the inventory team notifies the owning customer the same business day.

6.3 **Cycle counts.** Every SKU must be counted at least once every 30 days. SKUs whose last count is older than 30 days are flagged for counting in the next shift.

6.4 **Hazmat storage.** Hazmat SKUs may only be stored at facilities with hazmat docks (see Section 2.4).

## 7. Safety

7.1 High-visibility vests and safety footwear are required on the dock floor. Drivers must stay in the designated driver area unless directed by HPL staff.

7.2 Wheel chocks or a vehicle restraint must be engaged before any forklift enters a trailer.

7.3 Damaged or leaking hazmat packages are handled only by EHS-trained staff following HPL-EHS-004.

